   "name": "OH_Death",
   "description": "Death, from the owner-approved video: part 1 'fall-over' (refs/goblin-grunt-death/frames/fall-over, f01-f12) then part 2 'lying-still' (refs/goblin-grunt-death/frames/lying-still). Frames 0-75 follow fall-over f01-f12 (frame N of 12 = about N*6 frames): from the base pose he wobbles as if very dizzy (small sway of hips and spine, head lolls), knees buckle, he sits straight down onto his bottom on the spot (about f09-f10), then tips gently backwards onto his back (f11-f12), legs up a little then down. Frames 75-90 he settles flat on his back like lying-still f01-f04 (small bounce, arms fall loosely out to the sides, legs relax). Frames 90-120 he lies completely still in that pose (no breathing). Use \"move\" on the hips to lower him to the floor: the hips go straight DOWN (and slightly back) to lying height so his body rests ON the floor, never under it. He stays in his own square: no sliding, no rolling away; his hips end within about 15% of his height of where they started. He keeps holding his wooden board (frying-pan part) the whole time (it stays in his hand and lies flat on the floor beside him at the end, never through the floor). This clip does NOT return to idle: key every bone you use at the last frame (120) with the lying pose so the clip ends lying down.",
